                                "sense_id": "235351f5-9203-3c95-b7e8-976f00c0cbdf",
                                "text": "A salvor is a risktaker. […] The shores of Europe were littered with wrecks from the First World War. Sorima [la Società Ricuperi Marittimi] collected \"no cure, no pay\" (the equivalent of \"no win, no fee\") contracts from governments and insurers, seeking to recoup their losses."
                            }
